NAME
        bal asyncapi - Generate a Ballerina listener or client from an AsyncAPI contract,
                       or generate an AsyncAPI specification from Ballerina code.

SYNOPSIS
        bal asyncapi <input> --protocol <http|ws> [-o <dir>] [--module <name>] [--license <file>]
                     [--with-tests] [--service <base-path>] [--format <yaml|json>] [--force]
                     [--dry-run]

DESCRIPTION
        Generate Ballerina sources from the given AsyncAPI definition (.yaml, .yml or .json),
        or generate an AsyncAPI specification from Ballerina code. The direction is taken from
        the input: a definition generates code, a package directory or a .bal file generates
        a definition.

        Ballerina code is given as a package directory or as a standalone .bal file, the way
        'bal run' takes it. A .bal file that belongs to a package is not accepted; pass the
        package directory instead.

        Options a protocol does not support are reported as warnings and ignored.

        Existing files are never overwritten by default: a generated file that already exists
        with different content is skipped with a warning. Use --force to overwrite such files,
        and --dry-run to see what would be created, overwritten or skipped without writing.
        Files that already have the generated content are left untouched.

OPTIONS
        <input>
                Path to the AsyncAPI definition, or to the Ballerina package directory or
                standalone .bal file.

        --protocol <http|ws>
                Protocol of the AsyncAPI definition. Required.

        -o, --output <dir>
                Directory the generated files are written to. Defaults to the current directory.

        --module <name>
                Module of the Ballerina package to read services from, or to write generated
                code into. Not used with a standalone .bal file.

        --license <file>
                File with the license header placed on generated files (ws only).

        --with-tests
                Generate test files along with the code (ws only).

        --service <base-path>
                Base path of the service to generate the definition for, e.g. /chat. Every
                service with that base path is generated (Ballerina code input only).

        --format <yaml|json>
                Format of the generated AsyncAPI definition. Defaults to yaml (Ballerina code
                input only).

        --force
                Overwrite files that already exist in the output location. Without it, existing
                files are skipped with a warning.

        --dry-run
                Show which files would be created, overwritten or skipped, without writing
                anything.

        -h, --help
                Display this help.

EXAMPLES
        Generate a WebSocket client with tests.
            $ bal asyncapi chat.yaml --protocol ws --with-tests

        Generate an HTTP webhook listener into a module.
            $ bal asyncapi events.yaml --protocol http --module events -o ./pkg

        Preview what regenerating an HTTP listener would change, then apply it.
            $ bal asyncapi events.yaml --protocol http -o ./pkg --dry-run
            $ bal asyncapi events.yaml --protocol http -o ./pkg --force

        Generate the AsyncAPI definition of one service in a package, as JSON.
            $ bal asyncapi ./chat-package --protocol ws --service /chat --format json
